    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The issue seems to be that kwargs aren't considered when producing the args for compilation, this patch seems to fix it:\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/numba/cuda/dispatcher.py b/numba/cuda/dispatcher.py\r\n--- a/numba/cuda/dispatcher.py\r\n+++ b/numba/cuda/dispatcher.py\r\n@@ -763,6 +763,7 @@ class CUDADispatcher(Dispatcher, serialize.ReduceMixin):\r\n         # Ensure an exactly-matching overload is available if we can\r\n         # compile. We proceed with the typing even if we can't compile\r\n         # because we may be able to force a cast on the caller side.\r\n+        pysig, args = self._compiler.fold_argument_types(args, kws)\r\n         if self._can_compile:\r\n             self.compile_device(tuple(args))\r\n```\r\ncf. `_DispatcherBase`\r\nhttps://github.com/numba/numba/blob/f4b6fe0124fa7734ba2bb28c7685db5b6306c486/numba/core/dispatcher.py#L359\r\n",
