    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Notes from triage meeting:\r\n\r\n- There was a PR that attempted to add kwargs to CUDA, but I wasn't in support of the approach there, because it deviates from the core kwargs mechanism (#7871)\r\n- The above patch makes it look like argument folding works, but IIRC it will be incorrect if kwargs are in a different order in the parameter list to those in the declaration. I had an experiment with folding args (using a slightly different method to enable it) in https://github.com/gmarkall/numba/commit/1db1c44be1a541e73269ba12131762891d8410f5\r\n\r\nGiven that it is hard to make it work in general and maintain parity with the core dispatcher, we probably want to prevent kwargs being used for CUDA overloads.",
